WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.310
- You've heard all about it.

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.170
Apple's Vision Pro.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.930
It's the company's biggest
bet yet on a future

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.490
beyond the iPhone.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:09.546
Let's do this.

00:00:09.546 --> 00:00:12.930
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:16.440
Yes, I got my hands on it and
didn't take it off my face

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.910
for 24 hours.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.732
Oh, amazing.

00:00:19.732 --> 00:00:23.970
Or at least the better part of 24 hours.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:25.800
Ugh, that feels really nice.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.710
Ever since Apple announced
this headset, I've wondered

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:31.110
how is it going to fit in our lives?

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:33.540
We've already got screens everywhere.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.080
What does this $3,500
face computer do better?

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.040
Since I couldn't test it

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.140
for long stretches in my real house.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.140
Can you see my eyes?

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:43.919
- No.
(child mutters)

00:00:43.919 --> 00:00:46.320
- I headed to the Pocono Mountains
and rented this ski cabin

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.210
because what are these really,

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.880
if not super high tech ski goggles?

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:51.880
No one's gonna know.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.891
So it's noon, which is
the start of this journey.

00:00:56.891 --> 00:00:58.383
What could go wrong?

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.810
As soon as you put on the headset,

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.400
you see the real world.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.290
Right here is a grid of apps.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:08.430
The home screen.

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:10.530
You just look at what you wanna select,

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.810
then you use your hands to select it.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:17.580
Right now I'm looking at
settings, now App Store, Notes,

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.830
photos, Safari,

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:23.253
and to select one I just pinch.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:26.400
It's really intuitive.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.360
And to scroll, you just pinch and drag.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.540
The coolest thing is how you
can place apps all around you.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.910
Apple calls this spatial computing.

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:38.430
So I can start writing over here

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.290
in a document in front of me.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:43.050
I've got email over here on the left

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:46.140
and I've got music over here on the right.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:48.420
I was all set up to do some real work,

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.450
except one big problem.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:56.450
This is typing.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:58.080
Yeah, it's a struggle for anything

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.090
longer than a quick message.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:04.680
Thankfully, I have never been
so happy to see a keyboard.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.930
The real game changer
for getting work done.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.730
Adding in a Mac.

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:11.061
We are connected.

00:02:11.061 --> 00:02:14.490
Yes, you get a giant
desktop for your Mac apps

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:17.520
and you can run Vision Pro
apps right next to them.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:20.703
And you too can have this
for the low, low price of.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:24.720
But really, I continued
to work in the headset

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.183
for the next few hours and got a lot done.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:32.070
Next, I had to prepare my persona.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:37.070
Remove Apple Vision Pro to begin
capture, fix my hair, lips.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:38.043
Can I get a light?

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.640
- [Computer] Keep your
arms and shoulders relaxed.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.830
- See, when you video call in the headset,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.470
it can't capture your entire face.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:49.440
Most of the Vision Pro's
cameras are pointed outward.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.700
So Apple scans your face to
create a 3D stand-in for you.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.040
- [Computer] Smile with your mouth closed.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.270
Capture complete.

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:01.920
- It says creating persona.
What is going on with my cheeks?

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.350
- And when I FaceTime
people looking like this,

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.630
it was universally agreed upon.

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:08.010
- I think you look awful.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.440
- It's like Botox from hell.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.120
- They did you so dirty, dog.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.200
- What?

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:16.530
And yes, FaceTiming with
other people in Vision Pro is

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:18.501
as crazy as you'd think.

00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:22.950
Oh my goodness.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.680
Sure there's a lot of
remarkable tech here,

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.500
but can you really take
me seriously right now?

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:31.023
Apple says the persona feature is in beta.

00:03:31.859 --> 00:03:33.930
That persona scan is also used

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:36.839
to show your eyes on the front display

00:03:36.839 --> 00:03:37.950
so people know you're looking at them.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.410
But it can be hard to see.
I'm looking right at you.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:41.970
Now, it would be around this point

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:44.250
where most people would take
a break from this thing.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:47.190
I think it was the
combination of FaceTiming

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:48.300
and screen recording.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.280
But the top of this is very warm.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:53.740
I think it's time to switch
into the the dual loop band

00:03:56.407 --> 00:03:57.386
and feels pretty good.

00:03:57.386 --> 00:03:59.010
I ended up being happy that
Apple didn't strap this

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:00.630
thing's battery to my head.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.190
I got used to the hanging pack,

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:04.230
especially when I put it in this.

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:05.880
It's as cool as a Blackberry holster.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.970
I had to charge the battery
every two to three hours.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:12.090
So most of the time I just
stayed plugged into the wall,

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.250
but not for my next activity.

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:18.600
And here is our recipe, balsamic
mushroom and sausage pasta.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.300
Crouton is a recipe
app for the Vision Pro.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:22.890
So I put the window on one side

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:25.290
of the kitchen and got cooking.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:27.690
It is not recommended to
prepare food while wearing

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:29.190
the Apple Vision Pro.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:32.340
Okay, sure. Don't worry.

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:35.490
My producers were standing
by to make sure I was safe.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:37.440
Prepping food was really natural,

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.560
especially I could cut
onions all day in this.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.020
My eyes do not burn.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:45.990
This is amazing, but
the absolute best thing.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:47.850
So I see the timer here

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:51.390
and now I can move it over the pasta.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:55.020
And now I have a second
timer for six minutes

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:57.423
that I'm putting over the mushrooms.

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:01.290
This is just the coolest.

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:02.400
Was it perfect?

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.233
No.

00:05:03.233 --> 00:05:05.310
You're still looking at life on a screen.

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:06.143
In low light,

00:05:06.143 --> 00:05:07.770
I couldn't read things with smaller print

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:09.893
because of pixelation.

00:05:09.893 --> 00:05:12.390
Is there even Pepper coming
out? I cannot see it.

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:15.630
And some stuff just didn't
look like the right color,

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:18.510
but the display quality is far
better than the other leading

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.730
though far more affordable headset.

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:22.833
The $500 Meta Quest 3.

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:25.950
This is pretty much ready.

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:28.258
That's very good.

00:05:28.258 --> 00:05:29.950
(pensive music)

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:30.803
What should I watch?

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:36.180
Let's start with some Apple TV.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:38.550
You can create a giant
personal home theater

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:39.900
in the Vision Pro.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:40.733
Because of rights,

00:05:40.733 --> 00:05:42.630
I couldn't screen record the 2D

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:45.090
or 3D movies and shows that I watched.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:46.770
And even then seeing it in this video

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:48.540
wouldn't do it justice.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:52.350
There's Apple TV Plus, Disney
Plus and Paramount Plus,

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.570
but no Netflix or YouTube apps.

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:57.240
You have to watch those
through the browser.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:59.130
And the cinematic 3D virtual reality

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:00.630
videos Apple's offering.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.820
This is the kind of stuff
that makes me nauseous.

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:05.670
I do like one of the
virtual reality features.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:08.010
Turn the digital crown
on the top of the headset

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:10.500
and I am now

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:15.333
in 180 degree view of Yosemite.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.870
If you're like me and glasses on, you have

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:21.603
to get prescription inserts
to use The Vision Pro.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:24.723
I just click in like that.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:28.449
Wow. Crazy browser.

00:06:28.449 --> 00:06:32.493
Okay, I didn't sleep
with it. I'm not insane.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:34.953
Morning everyone.

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:38.308
(coffee dripping)

00:06:38.308 --> 00:06:39.420
That sounds delicious.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:42.240
Siri, what's the weather gonna be today?

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.790
- [Siri] 51 and a chance of Rain.

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:47.096
- Perfect skiing conditions.

00:06:47.096 --> 00:06:50.310
Let me be clear. No one
should ski with these on.

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:53.040
Apple's very explicit when
you first set up the headset

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.380
to only use it in safe areas.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:57.603
But I headed to Camelback anyway

00:06:57.603 --> 00:07:00.540
and worked with the mountain
to make sure the entire bunny

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.790
hill was closed off from others.

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:06.540
Hi. And I only wore them
briefly to record some video.

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:10.800
Siri record spatial video. Nope,
you gotta press the button.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:14.493
Poles on. Gloves on.

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:17.813
Here we go.

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:21.780
The Vision Pro's ability to record

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:24.630
and then watch Spatial or 3D images

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:27.030
and videos is pretty great.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:30.720
You can record spatial
video with an iPhone 15 Pro,

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.480
but hands-free recording
is one of the best uses

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:37.230
of connected eyewear like Meta's Ray Bans.

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:39.720
So what's it like wearing these for a day?

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:43.140
Painful, but also insightful.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:45.330
The Vision Pro has every characteristic

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:47.070
of a first generation product.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:49.350
It's heavy, it's battery life sucks.

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:51.060
There aren't that many great apps yet.

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:52.950
And sometimes it's bugged. No.

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.290
And oof. Personas.

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:58.320
But when you imagine a device
without those constraints,

00:07:58.320 --> 00:07:59.880
you see where it could be better than

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:01.740
holding a phone to your face.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:04.590
Vision Pro is a cooking computer.

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:05.423
For right now,

00:08:05.423 --> 00:08:08.790
it gives you a pretty great
way to work and watch movies.

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:11.340
Is that worth $3,500?

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.740
That's between you and your bank account.

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:15.030
But in those 24 hours,

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:17.790
I could see Apple's future vision here.

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:21.540
A pixelated yes, and a little
distorted glimpse of it.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:24.120
That is, where are you?

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:26.453
(laughing)

